    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d831">

                <pb facs="1065" n="963" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg963"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">681.003/142: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-30T17:00:00+00:00">January 30, 1935—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 30—1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>41. Embassy’s telegram 27,<anchor n="37" xml:id="d831-f1"/> Foreign Office
                    informs the Embassy as follows: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Notes regarding French Zone of Morocco and Tangier Zone were exchanged
                            with the French yesterday in London.</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>Arrangement is not to come into effect until a date to be fixed later
                            by mutual agreement.</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>Foreign Office states it will not consent to making the agreement on
                            the French Zone effective except simultaneously with those on the
                            Tangier Zone and Spanish Zone.</item>
                        <label>(4)</label>
                        <item>Agreement on the Tangier Zone must be approved by the Tangier
                            Legislative Assembly and the Tangier Committee of Control under the
                            Statute of 1923.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d831-f2"/>
                        </item>
                        <label>(5)</label>
                        <item>The agreement on the Spanish Zone has not yet been reached.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d831-f1" n="37" xml:id="d831-f1-content">
                <p>January 21, 6 p.m., <ref target="#pg1005">p. 1005</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d831-f2" n="38" xml:id="d831-f2-content">
                <p>Convention Regarding the Organization of the Statute of the Tangier Zone, signed
                    at Paris by France, Great Britain, and Spain, December 18, 1923, League of
                    Nations Treaty Series, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">xxviii</hi>, p. 541; for
                    correspondence concerning invitation to the United States to adhere to the
                    convention, see <ref target="frus1924v02#pg_456">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1924, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 456</ref>, and <ref
                        target="frus1925v02#pg_590">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 1925, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ii</hi>, p. 590</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
